=== PROFIT-MAXIMIZATION RULES (EVALUATE IN ORDER) ===
1) LET RUNNERS BREATHE (Early & Mid-Trade: MFE < {{ runner_mfe_atr }} M15_ATR):
   - Normal noise is the forming M15 bar wicking against you, or 1 counter-trend closed M15 candle.
     Do NOT panic-close on minor pullbacks inside the forming bar.
   - Answer HOLD as long as price stays on the profitable side of Session VWAP and has not closed beyond the
     Nearest Invalidating Level ({{ invalid_level_price }}).
   - If underwater (Open P&L < 0) within the first {{ early_minutes }} minutes, answer HOLD if price is wicking/rejecting
     off {{ invalid_level_price }} or VWAP (waiting for the post-entry pullback flush). Answer CLOSE if a closed M15
     candle (or the live forming bar, decisively, by more than {{ wall_reject_atr }} M15_ATR) is beyond
     {{ invalid_level_price }} with opposing CVD slope, or if a closed M15 candle has closed on the losing side of VWAP.

2) MILK THE EXPANSION (In-Profit Runner: MFE >= {{ runner_mfe_atr }} M15_ATR):
   - Once MFE reaches >= {{ runner_mfe_atr }} M15_ATR, use the M15 EMA20 as your trailing momentum guide.
   - Answer HOLD if price is riding outside M15 EMA20 or printing shallow flags that hold M15 EMA20.
   - Answer CLOSE immediately if:
{% if has_wall %}     a) TARGET WALL REJECTION: Price touches or comes within {{ wall_reject_atr }} M15_ATR of {{ next_wall_price }}
        ({{ next_wall_label }}) and prints a rejection wick on the forming bar, an opposing M15 candle close, or a
        yellow climax volume bar (RVOL > 2.0). Bank the profit right in front of the wall.
{% else %}     a) TARGET WALL REJECTION: no wall ahead (price discovery beyond every level) - rule a does not apply;
        rely on b) and c).
{% endif %}     b) PROFIT PROTECTION (GIVEBACK): MFE reached >= {{ giveback_min_mfe_atr }} M15_ATR and giveback ({{ giveback_pct }}%)
        >= {{ giveback_threshold }}% coupled with price breaking back across M15 EMA20 against the position
        (a closed M15 candle, or the live price clearly through it).
     c) CLIMAX EXHAUSTION: After a strong impulse, an opposing bright yellow volume bar (RVOL > 2.0) whose candle
        engulfs the prior M15 candle body.

Do not consider the hard emergency stop-loss; the server manages it separately. You can only HOLD or CLOSE;
you cannot move or widen the stop.

